Bash<pre><code>GET /health
</code></pre> <p>Response: JSON<pre><code>{
  "status": "healthy",
  "model_loaded": true
}
</code></pre></p>

Bash<pre><code>GET /v1/info
</code></pre> <p>Response: JSON<pre><code>{
  "model_version": "model-lr0.001-bs32-e50-20250121",
  "uptime_seconds": 12345.67
}
</code></pre></p>

Bash<pre><code>POST /v1/predict
</code></pre> <p>Request: Multipart form with image file</p> <p>Example: Bash<pre><code>curl -X POST https://drone-detector-api.../v1/predict \
  -F "file=@image.jpg"
</code></pre></p> <p>Response: JSON<pre><code>{
  "prediction": {
    "class_name": "drone",
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "scores": {
      "drone": 0.95,
      "bird": 0.05
    }
  },
  "metadata": {
    "inference_time_ms": 45.2,
    "model_version": "model-lr0.001-bs32-e50-20250121"
  }
}
</code></pre></p>

JSON<pre><code>{
  "detail": "Error message"
}
</code></pre> <p>Common status codes: - <code>400</code> - Invalid input - <code>413</code> - File too large - <code>500</code> - Server error</p>
